  "_reserved_memory_note": "Node selection accounts for ElastiCache's default reserved-memory-percent of 25%: the usable dataset capacity of a node is 0.75 x its advertised memory, and the chosen node's usable capacity meets or exceeds the plan's memory_limit (converted GB -> GiB). Examples: 25 GB (23.3 GiB) needs > 31 GiB advertised -> cache.m6g.4xlarge (52.26 GiB); 50 GB -> cache.m6g.8xlarge (103.68 GiB); 100 GB -> cache.m6g.12xlarge (157.12 GiB); 10 GB (9.3 GiB) fits cache.m6g.xlarge (12.93 GiB, 9.7 usable). An HA replica adds availability, not primary dataset capacity."
